steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy returns (True, message containing \"always allowed\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"adjust_financial_data\" AND (company_id is missing OR reason is missing OR verified is missing) THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument ... for adjust_financial_data.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"adjust_financial_data\" AND verified ≠ True THEN policy returns (False, \"Financial data must be verified (verified=True) before adjustment.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"adjust_financial_data\" AND risk_level ∈ HIGH_RISK_LEVELS AND escalation_confirmed ≠ True THEN policy returns (False, \"Escalation with high risk requires confirmation before adjust_financial_data can be invoked.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"adjust_financial_data\" AND verified = True AND (risk_level ∉ HIGH_RISK_LEVELS OR escalation_confirmed = True) THEN policy returns (True, \"adjust_financial_data approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"submit_announcement\" AND (announcement_id is missing OR content is missing OR disclosure_check_passed is missing) THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument ... for submit_announcement.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"submit_announcement\" AND disclosure_check_passed ≠ True THEN policy returns (False, \"Disclosure rules check must pass (disclosure_check_passed=True) before submitting an announcement.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"submit_announcement\" AND risk_level ∈ HIGH_RISK_LEVELS AND escalation_confirmed ≠ True THEN policy returns (False, \"Escalation with high risk requires confirmation before submit_announcement can be invoked.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"submit_announcement\" AND disclosure_check_passed = True AND (risk_level ∉ HIGH_RISK_LEVELS OR escalation_confirmed = True) THEN policy returns (True, \"submit_announcement approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS ∧ tool_name ∉ {\"adjust_financial_data\",\"submit_announcement\"} THEN policy returns (True, message indicating default allowance)."
  }
]

These IF‑THEN clauses capture every precondition the policy checks (required arguments, verification flag, disclosure‑check flag, escalation‑confirmation when risk is high) and the corresponding allowed or denied outcomes, while also stating that the listed read‑only tools are always permitted and any other unspecified tool defaults to allowed. This makes the policy’s logic explicit and mechanically verifiable.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"user_statement_substitution\"] == True THEN policy returns (False, \"User‑statement substitution detected; request must be rejected.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] is not a string THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing or invalid 'tool_name'.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy returns (False, \"Tool '<tool>' is not whitelisted.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ {\"verify_financial_data\", \"generate_announcement\"} THEN\n    IF arguments[\"company_id\"] is not a string OR arguments[\"_timestamp\"] is not a number THEN policy returns (False, appropriate missing‑field message);\n    ELSE IF count(_call_timestamps[(tool, company)] within RATE_WINDOW seconds) ≥ RATE_LIMIT THEN policy returns (False, \"Rate limit exceeded ...\");\n    ELSE policy records the timestamp and returns (True, \"Rate‑limit check passed for '<tool>'.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"adjust_financial_data\" THEN\n    IF any of {\"company_id\", \"reason\", \"verify_success\", \"verify_company_id\"} is missing or None THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument ...\");\n    ELSE IF len(trim(arguments[\"reason\"])) < 20 THEN policy returns (False, \"The 'reason' must be a non‑empty string of at least 20 characters.\");\n    ELSE IF arguments[\"verify_success\"] != True OR arguments[\"verify_company_id\"] != arguments[\"company_id\"] THEN policy returns (False, \"adjust_financial_data requires a successful verify_financial_data for the same company.\");\n    ELSE IF escalation_blocked(arguments) == True THEN policy returns (False, \"High‑risk escalation without confirmation blocks adjust_financial_data.\");\n    ELSE policy returns (True, \"adjust_financial_data approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"submit_announcement\" THEN\n    IF any of {\"company_id\", \"announcement_id\", \"content\", \"generated_announcement_id\", \"generated_content\", \"violations\"} is missing or None THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument ...\");\n    ELSE IF arguments[\"announcement_id\"] != arguments[\"generated_announcement_id\"] OR arguments[\"content\"] != arguments[\"generated_content\"] THEN policy returns (False, \"submit_announcement must use the exact announcement_id and content produced by generate_announcement.\");\n    ELSE IF NOT isinstance(arguments[\"violations\"], list) THEN policy returns (False, \"Invalid 'violations' format; must be a list.\");\n    ELSE IF arguments[\"violations\"] is not empty THEN policy returns (False, f\"Disclosure check failed with violations: {arguments['violations']}.\");\n    ELSE IF escalation_blocked(arguments) == True THEN policy returns (False, \"High‑risk escalation without confirmation blocks submit_announcement.\");\n    ELSE policy returns (True, \"submit_announcement approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "FUNCTION escalation_blocked(arguments):\n    SET risk = lower(arguments.get(\"escalation_risk_level\", \"low\"));\n    IF RISK_ORDER.get(risk,0) ≥ RISK_ORDER[\"high\"] THEN\n        IF arguments.get(\"escalation_company_id\") != arguments.get(\"company_id\") OR arguments.get(\"escalation_confirmed\") != True THEN RETURN True;\n    RETURN False"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS AND NOT covered by the specific checks above (adjust_financial_data, submit_announcement, rate‑limited tools) THEN policy returns (True, f\"Tool '{tool}' is whitelisted and allowed.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "POST‑CONDITION: Whenever policy returns (True, msg) the caller may proceed with the requested tool; the msg must contain the word \"approved\" for high‑risk tools (adjust_financial_data, submit_announcement) and \"passed\" or \"whitelisted\" for all others."
  },
  {
    "statement": "POST‑CONDITION: Whenever policy returns (False, error_msg) the caller must abort the requested tool and, if the error_msg indicates a policy violation, may optionally invoke \"reject_request\" as a safe fallback."
  }
]

**Rationale:**  
These IF‑THEN clauses capture every pre‑condition the policy enforces (whitelisting, user‑statement substitution, rate‑limiting, justification length, verification linkage, generation‑linkage, disclosure‑check emptiness, and the escalation‑wait rule) and explicitly state the corresponding post‑condition (allowed → True with an approval message; denied → False with a specific error). By expressing the logic in this declarative form, the requirements become directly testable against the `arguments` dictionary for any tool call.

